---
import Legal from '@/layouts/Legal.astro';
import { FOUNDING, LEGAL, PRICING } from '@/config/site';
---

<Legal title="Refunds & cancellation" description="Free trial, money-back guarantee, cancelling a subscription and the EU right of withdrawal.">
  <h2>Free trial</h2>
  <p>
    Godmode Pro (monthly or yearly) starts with a free {PRICING.trialDays}-day trial. Nothing is charged during the trial.
    Cancel before it ends — in the billing portal, from the app or by email — and you pay nothing at all. If you don’t
    cancel, the subscription starts automatically when the trial ends and your first month or year is charged then.
  </p>

  <h2>{PRICING.guaranteeDays}-day money-back guarantee</h2>
  <p>
    Not the right fit? Email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a> within {PRICING.guaranteeDays} days of
    your first payment (the first payment after the trial). We refund the full amount to your original payment method — no questions, no forms — and your license is
    deactivated.
  </p>

  <h2>Founding 100: {FOUNDING.outcomeHours} hours back, or every cent back</h2>
  <p>
    If you joined through the Founding 100 offer, you get a longer, outcome-based guarantee on top: set up at least
    {FOUNDING.setupAutomations} automations (we help on your setup call), and if Godmode hasn’t saved you
    {FOUNDING.outcomeHours} hours of work in the first {FOUNDING.outcomeDays} days after your first payment, email
    <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a> within those {FOUNDING.outcomeDays} days. We refund that payment in
    full; your own estimate of the time saved is enough. If your first automation isn’t running
    {FOUNDING.runningHours} hours after you install, tell us and the founder sets it up with you.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancelling a subscription</h2>
  <p>
    Cancel monthly or yearly plans anytime from the billing portal (linked in your receipt, on your welcome page and in the
    app) or by email. You keep access until the end of the month or year you’ve paid for; there are no further charges.
    Renewals are not refunded, except within the guarantee above.
  </p>

  <h2>Right of withdrawal for consumers in the EU</h2>
  <p>
    If you are a consumer, you have the right to withdraw from this contract within 14 days without giving any reason.
    The withdrawal period is 14 days from the day the contract is concluded. To exercise it, inform us
    ({LEGAL.company}, {LEGAL.street}, {LEGAL.city}, {LEGAL.country}, <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a>,
    {LEGAL.phone}) by a clear statement (e.g. an email). You may use the model form below, but you don’t have to. It is
    enough to send your notice before the period expires.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Consequences:</strong> if you withdraw, we refund all payments received from you without undue delay and at
    the latest within 14 days, using the same means of payment you used.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Early expiry for digital content:</strong> your right of withdrawal expires once we have started delivering the
    Software, if you expressly agreed that we begin before the withdrawal period ends and confirmed you know you lose
    your right of withdrawal this way. The voluntary money-back guarantee above still applies either way.
  </p>

  <h3>Model withdrawal form</h3>
  <p>
    To {LEGAL.company}, {LEGAL.street}, {LEGAL.city}, {LEGAL.country}, {LEGAL.email}:<br />
    I/We hereby give notice that I/we withdraw from my/our contract for the supply of the following digital content:
    Godmode ___ · Ordered on ___ · Name ___ · Address ___ · Date ___ · Signature (only on paper)
  </p>
</Legal>
